===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|lien||to lie, tell a falsehood}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lēogan||to lie}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*leugan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*leuganą||to lie}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-||to lie, swear, bemoan}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|lige||to lie}}, {{cog|nds|legen}}, {{m|nds|lögen||to lie}}, {{cog|nl|liegen||to lie}}, {{cog|de|lügen||to lie}}, {{cog|no|ljuge}}/{{m|no|lyge||to lie}}, {{cog|da|lyve||to lie}}, {{cog|sv|ljuga||to lie}}, and more distantly with {{cog|bg|лъжа||to lie}}, {{cog|pl|łgać||to lie}}, {{cog|ru|лгать||to lie}}, {{m|ru|ложь||falsehood}}.

