===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|lie}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lyġe||lie, falsehood}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*lugiz||lie, falsehood}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-||to tell lies, swear, complain}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|luggi||a lie}}, {{cog|goh|lugi|lugī}}, {{m|goh|lugin||a lie}} ({{cog|de|Lüge}}), {{cog|da|løgn||a lie}}, {{cog|bg|лъжа́||а lie}}, {{cog|ru|ложь||а lie}}, {{cog|cs|lež||a lie}}, {{cog|zlw-mpl|łeż||a lie}}, {{cog|sh|laž||a lie}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|intentional falsehood}} An [[intentionally]] [[false]] [[statement]]; an [[intentional]] [[falsehood]].
#: {{syn|en|alternative fact|deception|fabrication|falsehood|fib|leasing|nonsense|prevarication|tall tale|whopper|Thesaurus:lie}}
#: {{ant|en|truth}}
#: {{ux|en|I knew he was telling a '''lie''' by his facial expression.}}
#* {{RQ:Carlyle On Heroes|page=4|passage=Man everywhere is the born enemy of '''lies'''.}}
# A [[statement]] intended to [[deceive]], even if literally true.
#: {{syn|en|half-truth}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Anything that misleads or disappoints.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1835|author=w:Richard Chenevix Trench|title=the Story of Justin Martyr
|passage=Wishing this '''lie''' of life was o'er.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|year=2007|author=w:Erik Wolpaw; w:Chet Faliszek|title=[[w:Portal (video game)|Portal]]|text=The cake is a '''lie'''.}}

